WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.660
Good morning, John. I would like to do for you

00:00:02.660 --> 00:00:07.480
a historic reenactment of the moment when I read the title of your video from last week.

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:08.820
What a lovely day.

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:13.940
I am not currently experiencing any sources of broad anxiety. Let's go see if John's uploaded his video!

00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:19.480
HRRRRRRGGGGGGG-(segue into growling)

00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:21.780
I'm fine now. I mean how does this all end?

00:00:21.790 --> 00:00:25.630
It ends in death, John, you gave me a whole word for it that I forgot.

00:00:25.630 --> 00:00:31.080
It's gonna bug me, so I'm gonna text you. "What's the word for...the philosophical word for...

00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:34.460
death and talking about death that you use sometimes?"

00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:37.340
I mean the translation algorithms are getting so good now.

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:40.260
You know John, he'll write back. He knows what I mean.

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:44.740
First of all survey results say, people are cool with us taking three weeks of vacation.

00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:46.120
I don't know how I'm gonna do that.

00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:51.560
I'm not really set up for that, in my mind. There being space for flexibility...

00:00:51.560 --> 00:00:53.540
I don't know if that's good for me.

00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:55.600
I need to know exactly what I have to do.

00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:58.980
So I think that I'm going to schedule my vacation days,

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:01.320
like, very far in advance to not give myself the

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:05.020
possibility that like "Oh, maybe it's going to be this week if I don't have any good ideas".

00:01:05.020 --> 00:01:05.960
No, I need the pressure.

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:07.920
John, I think it's interesting that you were, like,

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:10.320
"how do we get a little bit of vacation?"

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:12.740
Where as I have spent the last three weeks being like

00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:16.380
"I think I need to upload a video about donuts on Hankschannel"

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:20.120
"What about the FDA's new nutritional label requirements?

00:01:20.120 --> 00:01:24.080
I think I need to weigh in on that." ‘Eschatology’. There's my big bro.

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:29.780
"Is the word you're thinking about, but it's the whole human apocalypse, not just individual death.

00:01:29.780 --> 00:01:33.720
Eschatological anxiety is fear of apocalyptic events." Oh!

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:36.040
But that stands, how is this going to end?

00:01:36.040 --> 00:01:41.100
You know, it will eventually. But I have a lot more to talk about today.  For example,

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:45.020
the fact that I have just left this hammer

00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:51.080
that I hit a router with on the floor for that long. It-- I have a problem...

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:53.880
with tidying up. Does anyone want this hammer?

00:01:53.880 --> 00:02:01.120
I'm gonna hide it in the bushes by the "Big Dipper" ice cream shop. And if you come by, it'll be there.

00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:04.960
OK. John, I'm almost done signing pieces of paper and the pieces of paper

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:09.900
they gave me for the UK editions of my book were different and had a weird cool

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:12.800
stop-motion effect when I sped up the video.

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:17.840
Each page is a little bit different, and the Carls fade in and out, and at one point, one of them blinks.

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:21.100
Whoever at Orion, which is my UK publisher, thought of that,

00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:26.280
that's amazing, and I did not expect that to work that well when you told me that you were doing it.

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:32.120
I was like, "Yeah, probably won't look as-- but it looks so cool!". Now, John, you just won't stop texting me about...

00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:37.540
various death... things. I also, John, have an audiobook narrator.

00:02:37.540 --> 00:02:41.760
I almost wish that I had been less involved beccause it gave me so much anxiety.

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:45.060
They were all so good, all of the people we had to choose from.

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:47.540
But ultimately, it was very subjective.

00:02:47.540 --> 00:02:52.440
It was the person, when I was listening to it, I felt like I was listening to April.

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:58.280
Gave me those goosebumps, made me feel like the person I created was talking to me.

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:03.290
Which was both, like, beautiful and emotional, but also, like, a little upsetting.

00:03:03.290 --> 00:03:07.600
And kind of uncanny, but the narrator of my audiobook, there's actually two of them.

00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:09.960
The main one is Kristen Sieh.

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:13.780
She was in "Orange is the New Black", "The Blacklist", "House of Cards".

00:03:13.780 --> 00:03:16.780
The other narrator of my audio book--

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:21.860
So there's, at a point in the book, a switching of perspectives for one chapter,

00:03:21.860 --> 00:03:23.000
and I will be doing...

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:24.600
that chapter.

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:27.360
And so I feel very good about this happening, and I cannot wait

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:30.580
to start getting into the weeds of getting the audiobook made.

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:32.660
And John, finally, to cap off this video,

00:03:32.660 --> 00:03:36.020
the comments that people left on your video, after you said this:

00:03:36.020 --> 00:03:38.380
"What do you get out of vlogbrothers videos?"

00:03:38.380 --> 00:03:42.240
were just so, like, life-giving to me.

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:45.040
I’ll know forever that if I need a little "lift me up", a little...

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:46.960
"kick me in the pants",

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:50.440
I can go to the comments of that video, and just read a little bit.

00:03:50.450 --> 00:03:52.040
So, thanks, John,

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:55.660
and thanks everybody who left those comments. It means a huge amount.

00:03:55.660 --> 00:03:57.020
John, I'll see you on Tuesday.

